  "@id": "https://w3id.org/pices/odis/records/zenodo-23519420.jsonld",
  "@type": "Dataset",
  "name": "Arctic Ice Dynamics Joint Experiment - Camp Data",
  "description": "During summer 1975, the Arctic Ice Dynamics Joint Experiment (AIDJEX) maintained 4 manned camps on ice floes in the Arctic Ocean. Instrumentation recorded surface and geostrophic winds, ocean current velocity at 2 and 30 meter depths, and camp (floe) position. Data available are daily average values for each parameter at each camp, as well as ice velocity and smoothed position data. Surface pressure and geostrophic wind data at 6-hourly intervals are also available.\n\nDeposited content: descriptive metadata only; underlying research data are not included.\n\nPurpose: To obtain data on instrumentation recorded surface and geostrophic winds, ocean current velocity at 2 and 30 meter depths, and camp (floe) position.",
  "url": "https://zenodo.org/records/23519421",
